@prefix sh:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix shp:  <http://fairmat-nfdi.eu/taxonomy/shapes/units#> .
@prefix rep:  <http://fairmat-nfdi.eu/taxonomy/representation#> .
@prefix tax:  <http://fairmat-nfdi.eu/taxonomy/> .
@prefix qb:   <http://purl.org/linked-data/cube#> .
@prefix qudt: <http://qudt.org/2.1/schema/qudt/> .
@prefix qk:   <http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/> .
@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .

<http://fairmat-nfdi.eu/taxonomy/shapes/units> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:comment """Shapes graph for the rep:hasUnit layer of the representation module.

Scope: units only. Rank, axis cardinality and canonical-axis membership
are not validated by this graph; they belong in a future structural
shapes graph.

WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. representation.ttl gives every component a
rep:hasUnit edge, so a unit can be STATED. It cannot constrain WHICH:
"a Length axis is never measured in seconds" is a closed-world statement
and OWL has no closed world. HermiT accepts unit:SEC on rep:depth without
complaint. Every permitted-unit set therefore lives here and only here --
the TBox declares six unit individuals and says nothing about pairing.

TWO LAYERS.

  Layer 1  DIMENSIONAL    sh:Violation
           The unit must be a permitted unit for the component's own
           quantity kind. Driven by the shp:permitsUnit map below, not
           hard-coded into a shape. Adding a unit to the vocabulary is
           one triple.

  Layer 2  PROFILE        sh:Warning
           The unit must sit inside the narrower set conventional for
           this representation type. unit:MicroM on a DepthProfile depth axis
           is dimensionally correct and off-profile -- it passes Layer 1
           and warns at Layer 2. This is the distinction that makes a
           severity split worth having: Layer 1 means the data is wrong,
           Layer 2 means the data is unusual.

           Layer 2 is needed because qk:Length covers both the nm-scale
           depth axis and the um-scale image axes. The quantity kind
           alone cannot separate them; the representation type can.

STRUCTURED ERRORS. Every shape carries shp:code, shp:category,
shp:layer and shp:remedy. A validation report references its shape
through sh:sourceShape, so a consumer joins report -> shape -> metadata
and gets a stable machine-readable code instead of parsing prose out of
sh:resultMessage. See test/representation_test.py, which does exactly
that join.

PLACEMENT. rep:hasUnit is legal on two subjects (see the TBox domain):
the canonical rep:ComponentProperty individual, carrying the module
default, and the qb:ComponentSpecification, carrying the dataset-scoped
actual. Layer 1 targets sh:targetSubjectsOf rep:hasUnit and so covers
both without a second shape. Layer 2 is dataset-scoped by nature and
targets ComponentSpecifications reached from a typed dataset."""@en .

#################################################################
##  0. ERROR METADATA VOCABULARY
##
##  Annotation properties on shapes. They carry no SHACL semantics
##  -- the engine ignores them -- and exist so a report consumer
##  can resolve sh:sourceShape to a stable code.
#################################################################

shp:code     a owl:AnnotationProperty ; rdfs:comment "Stable error code, e.g. REP-UNIT-001."@en .
shp:category a owl:AnnotationProperty ; rdfs:comment "dimensional | profile | cardinality | typing."@en .
shp:layer    a owl:AnnotationProperty ; rdfs:comment "1 = dimensional (hard), 2 = profile (advisory)."@en .
shp:remedy   a owl:AnnotationProperty ; rdfs:comment "What the producer should do about it."@en .

#################################################################
##  1. THE UNIT MAP  --  shp:permitsUnit
##
##  Layer 1 is driven by a table, not by shape logic. Extending the
##  permitted vocabulary is adding one triple here; no shape is edited.
##
##  THIS TABLE IS A SNAPSHOT AND WILL GROW WITHOUT NOTICE. The sets
##  below are current as of September 2026 and list only what the
##  module's own six representation types use today -- one unit per
##  quantity kind, except length, which needs two because a depth
##  axis works in nanometres and an image axis in micrometres.
##
##  They are not a claim about which units exist, nor a closed
##  statement about what QUDT offers for these kinds. Kinds will gain
##  units and new kinds will be added as more instrument classes come
##  in, and that will happen without an announcement. Growth is the
##  normal operating mode of this table, not an exception. Each
##  addition is one triple: no shape edit, no TBox change.
##
##  Note the table currently matches the six unit individuals declared
##  in representation.ttl exactly. That is a coincidence of the
##  starting point, not an invariant -- the moment a dataset needs
##  millimetres, this table grows and the TBox does not.
##
##  IMPORTANT -- THIS FILE MUST BE LOADED INTO THE DATA GRAPH TOO.
##  The FILTER NOT EXISTS in REP-UNIT-001 is evaluated against the
##  data graph. pyshacl's ont_graph parameter does not reliably mix
##  it in; passed that way the constraint fires on every well-formed
##  component. test/representation_test.py loads this file twice --
##  once as the shapes graph, once alongside the TBox as data. The
##  shapes themselves are inert as data: nothing targets them.
##
##  The table is also useful outside validation:
##
##      SELECT ?u WHERE { qk:Length shp:permitsUnit ?u }
##
##  answers "what may I write for a length axis" with no validator.
##
##  These unit IRIs are deliberately NOT in representation.ttl. The
##  TBox holds the six canonical defaults; the wider set a dataset
##  may legitimately use is a closed-world fact and belongs here.
#################################################################

shp:permitsUnit a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain qudt:QuantityKind ;
    rdfs:range  qudt:Unit ;
    rdfs:comment "Unit U is dimensionally admissible for quantity kind K."@en .

qk:Temperature shp:permitsUnit unit:K .

qk:Length      shp:permitsUnit unit:NanoM , unit:MicroM .

qk:Time        shp:permitsUnit unit:SEC .

qk:Energy      shp:permitsUnit unit:EV .

tax:Intensity  shp:permitsUnit unit:COUNT .

### typing for the units named above, so sh:class qudt:Unit resolves
unit:K a qudt:Unit .  unit:NanoM a qudt:Unit .  unit:MicroM a qudt:Unit .
unit:SEC a qudt:Unit .  unit:EV a qudt:Unit .  unit:COUNT a qudt:Unit .

#################################################################
##  2. LAYER 1  --  DIMENSIONAL AGREEMENT   (sh:Violation)
#################################################################

###  REP-UNIT-001
###  The unit must be permitted for the subject's quantity kind.
###
###  One shape covers both placements. The kind is reached either
###  directly (canonical individual: it carries hasQuantityKind
###  itself) or by one hop through qb:dimension / qb:measure
###  (ComponentSpecification: the kind lives on the component it
###  points at). SPARQL is required because SHACL Core cannot
###  compare the values of two different paths.
###
###  The SELECT binds ?value deliberately: SHACL-SPARQL lifts a bound
###  ?value into sh:value on the result, so the report names the
###  offending unit rather than repeating the focus node.

shp:UnitKindAgreementShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    shp:code "REP-UNIT-001" ;
    shp:category "dimensional" ;
    shp:layer 1 ;
    shp:remedy "Use a unit listed by shp:permitsUnit for this quantity kind, or correct rep:hasQuantityKind." ;
    sh:severity sh:Violation ;
    sh:targetSubjectsOf rep:hasUnit ;
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "REP-UNIT-001 dimensional: unit {?value} is not admissible for quantity kind {?kind}." ;
        sh:prefixes <http://fairmat-nfdi.eu/taxonomy/shapes/units> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT $this ?value ?kind
            WHERE {
                $this rep:hasUnit ?value .
                {
                    $this rep:hasQuantityKind ?kind .
                } UNION {
                    $this qb:dimension ?comp .
                    ?comp rep:hasQuantityKind ?kind .
                } UNION {
                    $this qb:measure ?comp .
                    ?comp rep:hasQuantityKind ?kind .
                }
                FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?kind shp:permitsUnit ?value }
            }
        """ ] .

###  REP-UNIT-002
###  The object of rep:hasUnit must be a unit, not a quantity kind.
###  Swapping the two is the single most common authoring slip,
###  and Layer 1 alone would report it as a confusing "not
###  admissible for kind" rather than naming the real mistake.

shp:UnitIsNotAKindShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    shp:code "REP-UNIT-002" ;
    shp:category "typing" ;
    shp:layer 1 ;
    shp:remedy "Replace the qudt:QuantityKind with the corresponding qudt:Unit individual." ;
    sh:severity sh:Violation ;
    sh:targetObjectsOf rep:hasUnit ;
    sh:not [ sh:class qudt:QuantityKind ] ;
    sh:message "REP-UNIT-002 typing: object of rep:hasUnit is a qudt:QuantityKind. A unit was expected." .

#################################################################
##  3. LAYER 1  --  CARDINALITY   (sh:Violation)
##
##  Scoped to ComponentSpecifications inside a DSD. Every slot a
##  dataset declares must state exactly one unit. rep:hasUnit is
##  owl:FunctionalProperty, but functional means "any two values
##  are the same individual", which under OWL infers owl:sameAs
##  rather than rejecting -- so maxCount is not redundant here.
#################################################################

shp:ComponentSpecUnitCardinalityShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    shp:code "REP-UNIT-003" ;
    shp:category "cardinality" ;
    shp:layer 1 ;
    shp:remedy "State exactly one rep:hasUnit on every qb:ComponentSpecification." ;
    sh:severity sh:Violation ;
    sh:targetSubjectsOf qb:dimension ;
    sh:targetSubjectsOf qb:measure ;
    sh:property [
        sh:path rep:hasUnit ;
        sh:severity sh:Violation ;
        sh:minCount 1 ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:nodeKind sh:IRI ;
        sh:message "REP-UNIT-003 cardinality: a qb:ComponentSpecification must carry exactly one rep:hasUnit." ] .

#################################################################
##  4. LAYER 2  --  PER-TYPE PROFILES   (sh:Warning)
##
##  SPARQL targets, because the constraint is keyed on the
##  representation type of the DATASET while the unit sits on a
##  ComponentSpecification two hops away. A Core sequence path
##  would reach the unit but could not restrict to axis slots
##  versus signal slots.
##
##  Profiles, from the canonical vocabulary:
##
##    Scalar        signal temperature   K
##    Spectrum      axis   energy        EV
##    TimeSeries    axis   time          SEC
##    DepthProfile  axis   depth         NanoM
##    Image         axis   y, x          MicroM, NanoM
##    VolumeData    axis   z, y, x       MicroM, NanoM
##    any           signal intensity     COUNT
#################################################################

shp:ScalarTemperatureUnitShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    shp:code "REP-UNIT-010" ;
    shp:category "profile" ;
    shp:layer 2 ;
    shp:remedy "Scalar temperature is reported in unit:K." ;
    sh:severity sh:Warning ;
    sh:target [
        a sh:SPARQLTarget ;
        sh:prefixes <http://fairmat-nfdi.eu/taxonomy/shapes/units> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT ?this WHERE {
                ?ds a rep:Scalar ; qb:structure ?dsd .
                ?dsd qb:component ?this .
                ?this qb:measure ?c .
                ?c rep:hasQuantityKind qk:Temperature .
            }
        """ ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:path rep:hasUnit ;
        sh:severity sh:Warning ;
        sh:in ( unit:K ) ;
        sh:message "REP-UNIT-010 profile: Scalar temperature outside the K profile." ] .

shp:SpectrumEnergyAxisUnitShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    shp:code "REP-UNIT-011" ;
    shp:category "profile" ;
    shp:layer 2 ;
    shp:remedy "Spectrum energy axes are reported in unit:EV." ;
    sh:severity sh:Warning ;
    sh:target [
        a sh:SPARQLTarget ;
        sh:prefixes <http://fairmat-nfdi.eu/taxonomy/shapes/units> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT ?this WHERE {
                ?ds a rep:Spectrum ; qb:structure ?dsd .
                ?dsd qb:component ?this .
                ?this qb:dimension ?c .
            }
        """ ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:path rep:hasUnit ;
        sh:severity sh:Warning ;
        sh:in ( unit:EV ) ;
        sh:message "REP-UNIT-011 profile: Spectrum axis outside the eV profile." ] .

shp:TimeSeriesAxisUnitShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    shp:code "REP-UNIT-012" ;
    shp:category "profile" ;
    shp:layer 2 ;
    shp:remedy "TimeSeries axes are reported in unit:SEC." ;
    sh:severity sh:Warning ;
    sh:target [
        a sh:SPARQLTarget ;
        sh:prefixes <http://fairmat-nfdi.eu/taxonomy/shapes/units> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT ?this WHERE {
                ?ds a rep:TimeSeries ; qb:structure ?dsd .
                ?dsd qb:component ?this .
                ?this qb:dimension ?c .
            }
        """ ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:path rep:hasUnit ;
        sh:severity sh:Warning ;
        sh:in ( unit:SEC ) ;
        sh:message "REP-UNIT-012 profile: TimeSeries axis outside the s profile." ] .

shp:DepthProfileAxisUnitShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    shp:code "REP-UNIT-013" ;
    shp:category "profile" ;
    shp:layer 2 ;
    shp:remedy "Depth axes are reported in unit:NanoM. Micrometres are a valid length unit but far off the scale of a depth profile -- check for a units-of-convenience error." ;
    sh:severity sh:Warning ;
    sh:target [
        a sh:SPARQLTarget ;
        sh:prefixes <http://fairmat-nfdi.eu/taxonomy/shapes/units> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT ?this WHERE {
                ?ds a rep:DepthProfile ; qb:structure ?dsd .
                ?dsd qb:component ?this .
                ?this qb:dimension ?c .
            }
        """ ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:path rep:hasUnit ;
        sh:severity sh:Warning ;
        sh:in ( unit:NanoM ) ;
        sh:message "REP-UNIT-013 profile: DepthProfile axis outside the nm profile." ] .

shp:ImageAxisUnitShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    shp:code "REP-UNIT-014" ;
    shp:category "profile" ;
    shp:layer 2 ;
    shp:remedy "Image axes are reported in unit:MicroM or unit:NanoM." ;
    sh:severity sh:Warning ;
    sh:target [
        a sh:SPARQLTarget ;
        sh:prefixes <http://fairmat-nfdi.eu/taxonomy/shapes/units> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT ?this WHERE {
                ?ds a rep:Image ; qb:structure ?dsd .
                ?dsd qb:component ?this .
                ?this qb:dimension ?c .
            }
        """ ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:path rep:hasUnit ;
        sh:severity sh:Warning ;
        sh:in ( unit:MicroM unit:NanoM ) ;
        sh:message "REP-UNIT-014 profile: Image axis outside the um / nm profile." ] .

shp:VolumeAxisUnitShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    shp:code "REP-UNIT-015" ;
    shp:category "profile" ;
    shp:layer 2 ;
    shp:remedy "VolumeData axes are reported in unit:MicroM or unit:NanoM." ;
    sh:severity sh:Warning ;
    sh:target [
        a sh:SPARQLTarget ;
        sh:prefixes <http://fairmat-nfdi.eu/taxonomy/shapes/units> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT ?this WHERE {
                ?ds a rep:VolumeData ; qb:structure ?dsd .
                ?dsd qb:component ?this .
                ?this qb:dimension ?c .
            }
        """ ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:path rep:hasUnit ;
        sh:severity sh:Warning ;
        sh:in ( unit:MicroM unit:NanoM ) ;
        sh:message "REP-UNIT-015 profile: VolumeData axis outside the um / nm profile." ] .

shp:IntensitySignalUnitShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    shp:code "REP-UNIT-016" ;
    shp:category "profile" ;
    shp:layer 2 ;
    shp:remedy "Uncalibrated intensity is reported in unit:COUNT." ;
    sh:severity sh:Warning ;
    sh:target [
        a sh:SPARQLTarget ;
        sh:prefixes <http://fairmat-nfdi.eu/taxonomy/shapes/units> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT ?this WHERE {
                ?dsd qb:component ?this .
                ?this qb:measure ?c .
                ?c rep:hasQuantityKind tax:Intensity .
            }
        """ ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:path rep:hasUnit ;
        sh:severity sh:Warning ;
        sh:in ( unit:COUNT ) ;
        sh:message "REP-UNIT-016 profile: intensity signal outside the count profile." ] .

#################################################################
##  5. PREFIX DECLARATIONS FOR sh:prefixes
##
##  SHACL-SPARQL does not inherit Turtle prefixes. Every
##  sh:select above references this node.
#################################################################

<http://fairmat-nfdi.eu/taxonomy/shapes/units>
    sh:declare [ sh:prefix "rep"  ; sh:namespace "http://fairmat-nfdi.eu/taxonomy/representation#"^^xsd:anyURI ] ;
    sh:declare [ sh:prefix "tax"  ; sh:namespace "http://fairmat-nfdi.eu/taxonomy/"^^xsd:anyURI ] ;
    sh:declare [ sh:prefix "shp"  ; sh:namespace "http://fairmat-nfdi.eu/taxonomy/shapes/units#"^^xsd:anyURI ] ;
    sh:declare [ sh:prefix "qb"   ; sh:namespace "http://purl.org/linked-data/cube#"^^xsd:anyURI ] ;
    sh:declare [ sh:prefix "qudt" ; sh:namespace "http://qudt.org/2.1/schema/qudt/"^^xsd:anyURI ] ;
    sh:declare [ sh:prefix "qk"   ; sh:namespace "http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/"^^xsd:anyURI ] ;
    sh:declare [ sh:prefix "unit" ; sh:namespace "http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/"^^xsd:anyURI ] .
